Collective Variables - ACE-CYS-NME Metadynamics
=====================================================
System: ACE-CYS-NME (23 atoms), vacuum, 300 K
Force field: AMBER ff14SB (amber14sb.xml), NoCutoff
Platform: OpenMM Reference

CV1 = phi (backbone dihedral):
  Atoms: C(ACE) - N(CYS) - CA(CYS) - C(CYS)
  PDB serials (1-based): 5, 7, 9, 16
  0-based indices: 4, 6, 8, 15
  Periodicity: 360 degrees
  Range: [-180, 180)

CV2 = psi (backbone dihedral):
  Atoms: N(CYS) - CA(CYS) - C(CYS) - N(NME)
  PDB serials (1-based): 7, 9, 16, 18
  0-based indices: 6, 8, 15, 17
  Periodicity: 360 degrees
  Range: [-180, 180)

Rationale:
  The system is a single CYS residue flanked by standard ACE (N-terminal
  acetyl) and NME (C-terminal N-methyl) caps. The only backbone
  conformational degrees of freedom are the phi and psi dihedrals of the
  CYS residue. These two angles fully span the Ramachandran conformational
  space of the peptide backbone. No other backbone dihedrals exist in this
  topology. The side-chain chi1 (N-CA-CB-SG) is not a backbone angle and
  is excluded from the 2D FES.

Metadynamics parameters:
  Flavour:       Well-tempered metadynamics
  Delta:         5.0 kJ/mol
  Gaussian H0:   1.0 kJ/mol
  Gaussian sigma: 5.0 degrees
  Deposition:    every 100 MD steps (0.2 ps at 2 fs timestep)
  Timestep:      2 fs
  Temperature:   300 K
  Integrator:    Langevin (friction = 1/ps)
  Total length:  100 ns (50,000,000 steps)

FES grid:
  Resolution:    72 x 72
  Range:         [-180, 180) degrees on both axes
  Cell width:    5 degrees
  Cell centres:  -177.5, -172.5, ..., +177.5 degrees

FES reconstruction:
  Primary:  Direct reweighting F(s) = -kT * ln[P(s) * exp(V(s)/kT)]
  Fallback: Bias-only F(s) = -(kT+Delta) * ln[V(s)/V_max]
  where P(s) is the normalised histogram of sampled (phi, psi) values
  and V(s) is the summed bias potential on the grid.
  No built-in FES retrieval functions used.
